BUG-003 reproduction test, 2026-11-14
=====================================

Question: does `ContentId: rbxassetid://203785492 failed due to: Asset type does not match
requested type` come from this project's place, or from Studio/cloud?

Method
------
A throwaway place containing nothing but three empty services was written by hand at
%TEMP%\opencode\blank-probe.rbxlx (`Workspace`, `Lighting`, `Players`, no scripts, no Rojo sync,
no StarterGui, no models, no asset references of any kind) and opened in a second Studio instance:

    RobloxStudioBeta.exe -task EditFile -localPlaceFile %TEMP%\opencode\blank-probe.rbxlx

MCP reported it as `persistedToCloud: false`, `placeId` absent, unlike the project place
(`persistedToCloud: true`, placeId 132087524375529).

Play was started on the blank place; the first console read immediately after the start returned
empty (`null`). After a further 6 seconds of play the console read:

```
ContentId: rbxassetid://203785492 failed due to: Asset type does not match requested type
ContentId: rbxassetid://203785492 failed due to: Asset type does not match requested type
ContentId: rbxassetid://203785492 failed due to: Asset type does not match requested type
```

That is the same three lines, three times, from a place with no content at all.

Conclusion
----------
BUG-003 is external to this project. A place with no scripts and no asset references reproduces it,
and the earlier sweep showed the id is in no file, no Roblox binary and no registry value on this
machine. It is emitted by Studio or the account/cloud during play start, so no change in this repo
can remove it. Track C is clear of it; the "zero warnings" bar is judged with this line excluded.
